# Infra + deploy rules

The deploy is **CodeBuild-owned**, not Terraform-owned. The pipeline is
Source → Build → Deploy, all wired in `packages/terraform-aws/cicd.tf`.

Hard rules:

- The ECS task definition is the single source of truth at
  `apps/api/taskdef.template.json`. Terraform reads the latest active
  revision via `data "aws_ecs_task_definition" "api"` only — do NOT add an
  `aws_ecs_task_definition` resource back.
- `aws_ecs_service.api` keeps `lifecycle { ignore_changes = [task_definition] }`.
  Don't remove it; CodeBuild rolls revisions every deploy.
- Images are tagged with the full commit SHA. Never push or deploy `:latest`.
- New runtime env vars require BOTH (a) a placeholder in
  `apps/api/taskdef.template.json` AND (b) a matching `environment_variable`
  in the `aws_codebuild_project.api_deploy` resource so `envsubst` can fill
  it in. Secret vars also need an SSM parameter and the deploy role's
  policy must allow `ssm:GetParameters` on its ARN.
- Base images (Bun, Postgres) are pulled from the ECR mirror
  (`hirely-prod-base/bun`, `public.ecr.aws/docker/library/postgres`) to
  avoid Docker Hub rate limits in CodeBuild. Don't switch back to
  `oven/bun` or `library/postgres` on Docker Hub.
- Never commit `terraform.tfvars` or `*.tfstate*`. They are gitignored for a
  reason.
